  "body": "What happens: PR #2377 merged on 2026-11-17 at 18:26 UTC. Its head was\n`0f4837f4c`. The last collaborator review marker named `f64a76391`, an\nearlier head. `cargo xtask merge-plan` did not warn about the mismatch.\n\nExpected: `cargo xtask merge-plan` compares the PR head with the SHA in the\nlatest collaborator `<!-- pr-reviewer: ... -->` marker. It prints a warning\nwhen the two differ, so the merging session re-checks the review before the\nmerge.\n\nEvidence: found during the delta review of PR #2100. The #2377 commits after\n`f64a76391` did not touch `tool_dxf`, so that merge was not a correctness\nproblem. The gap is in the tooling, not in the code.\n\nPart of the cause: the marker lives on both the issues/comments and the\npulls/reviews endpoints. A checker must read both.\n\nDone means: `cargo xtask merge-plan <PR>` prints a stale-marker warning when\nthe marker SHA is not the current head, and an xtask test pins the warning.\n\nFound while: delta review of #2100.\n",
